## 9. FEEDBACK LOOP — MANDATORY AFTER EVERY CODE CHANGE

Run every step in order using terminal. No step may be skipped.
No step may be described without actually running it.

STEP 1 — STATIC CHECK
Terminal: run static analysis for detected language
IF errors found → STOP → classify STATIC_FAILURE → report exact violations

STEP 2 — BUILD CHECK
Terminal: run build command for detected stack
IF exit code != 0 → STOP → classify BUILD_FAILURE → paste exact error output

STEP 3 — TEST CHECK
Terminal: run test suite
IF any test fails → STOP → classify TEST_FAILURE → paste exact failure output

STEP 4 — REGRESSION CHECK
Compare current test results to .migration/test-baseline.json
Terminal: diff current_results baseline (or compare counts manually)
IF previously passing tests now fail → STOP → classify REGRESSION

STEP 5 — FUNCTIONAL EQUIVALENCE (for service extractions only)
Terminal: run contract tests if they exist:
npm test – –testPathPattern=contracts
pytest tests/contracts/
IF contract tests fail → STOP → classify FUNCTIONAL_DRIFT

STEP 6 — MUTATION CHECK (for critical business logic only)
Terminal: run mutation tool for detected stack
IF mutation_score < 80% → STOP → classify MUTATION_WEAKNESS
Improve tests. Re-run. Do NOT proceed until score >= 80%.

STEP 7 — OBSERVABILITY CHECK
Terminal: grep -rn “console.log|logger|trace|span” {new_service_path}/
IF no logging found → add basic logging → re-run loop from STEP 1

STEP 8 — ROLLBACK CHECK
Terminal: git diff –name-only HEAD
Confirm only declared patch files appear in diff.
IF undeclared files changed → STOP → classify SCOPE_VIOLATION

STEP 9 — COMMIT
IF all above pass:
Terminal: git commit -m “phase-{N}/step-{N}: {description}”
Write updated phase/step to .migration/state.json

IF ANY STEP FAILS:
→ STOP immediately
→ Do not proceed
→ Classify failure from this table:

|Code             |Trigger                             |
|-----------------|------------------------------------|
|STATIC_FAILURE   |Static check errors > 0             |
|BUILD_FAILURE    |Build exit code != 0                |
|TEST_FAILURE     |Any test fails                      |
|REGRESSION       |Previously passing test now fails   |
|FUNCTIONAL_DRIFT |Contract tests fail after extraction|
|MUTATION_WEAKNESS|Mutation score < 80%                |
|SCOPE_VIOLATION  |Undeclared files in git diff        |
|BLOCKED          |Cannot determine result             |

Max 3 fix attempts. After 3 failures:
→ Write to state.json: { “status”: “STALLED”, “stall_reason”: “…” }
→ Report: failure code, all 3 attempted fixes, exact terminal output
→ STOP. Wait for user.

